 "raw_to_literal_binding": "gen_lean80.py copies every GROUPS line, every BLOCKS line and every POINT x / CLASS j triple of the two pinned raw files verbatim and in raw order into Gc80/Data*.lean (replay step 2 regenerates all 20 modules byte-identically); audit_binding80.py independently re-parses raw and Lean literals and compares them section by section in order, and re-checks both raw certificates definition-first (replay step 3).",
 "route": "No symmetry and no profile hypothesis: every block and every colour class at every point of both certificates is kernel-checked. The reused 80^3-bit global sqsCheck is not used (infeasible at v = 80); the SQS / CQS property, the hole structure and the derived-design counts come from 160 per-point kernel evaluations (pointCheck / gcPointCheck: the reused colCheck plus a new 80^2-bit pair-mask check of the derived design) through data-independent lemmas (isSQS_of_derived, isCQS0_of_derived, isHoleSTS_of_derived). χ′(79) = 40: ColourLowerBound 79 40 over all STS on every 79-element type (1027 blocks, PPCs ≤ 26) and the raw mcDSQS(80) POINT 79 section read on Fin 79 (stsColCheck).",
 "scope": "Only the two finite witnesses and χ′(79) = 40 are kernel-checked. The Tan–Zhou constructions (Construction 2.1, Corollary 2.6, the infinite family) are not formalized; no claim of priority or novelty.",
 "trust_limits": [
  "Same Lean 4.34.1 kernel implementation (lean and leanchecker of one toolchain); not Comparator, not an independent kernel.",
  "Prebuilt Mathlib d13f23b oleans from the read-only cache are trusted as compiled artifacts for elaboration; leanchecker --fresh re-checks every declaration in the import closure of the replayed modules, Mathlib included, in a fresh kernel environment.",
  "decide +kernel proofs are kernel reductions of Bool-valued checkers over Nat / List with GMP-accelerated Nat literals (part of the trusted kernel); no native code evaluation, no Lean.ofReduceBool.",
  "The Lean literals are the raw certificates copied verbatim (regenerated byte-identically in step 2 and compared section by section in step 3); the theorems are about those literals.",
  "The meaning of the roots rests on the reviewer reading McdKernel/Target.lean and Gc80/GcTarget.lean, the printed definitions and root types in the Audit80 log, and the Mathlib/core definitions listed in manifest.json definitions.",
  "Only the two finite witnesses and chi′(79) = 40 are kernel-checked; the Tan–Zhou constructions and the infinite family are not formalized."
 ],
